1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,340
KIAN'S B&B

2
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:09,050
Should I carry you on my shoulders?

3
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:09,968
What do we do?

4
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:11,553
You carry her on your shoulders.

5
00:00:11,636 --> 00:00:12,929
Should I?

6
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:15,223
SHE GIVES IT A TRY WITHOUT HESITATION

7
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:16,933
Let's do it.

8
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:18,518
Look at her posture.

9
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:20,520
- You have to go lower. Yeah.
- Lower?

10
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:21,730
- Yeah. Give it a try.
- Wait.

11
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:24,899
- She says she works out a lot.
- Hold onto me.

12
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:25,984
- Hold onto me.
- Okay.

13
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:27,444
Hold on.

14
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:29,696
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

15
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:34,868
- It's working.
- It's working.

16
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:36,536
Come on. Hurry.

17
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:38,955
- Hurry.
- I got it.

18
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:40,874
- You got it?
- Yeah.

19
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:46,087
Three! Okay.

20
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,130
Hey, Zuha!

21
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:48,047
Hey, be careful.

22
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:49,966
Wait!

23
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:50,884
It's open now.

24
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,886
- Let her down.
- Let her down.

25
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:54,179
Hey, Zuha.

26
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,389
- Good job.
- Hey!

27
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,307
Hey, you're strong.

28
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,808
- Hey.
- I didn't think I could do it.

29
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,019
She's unbelievable!

30
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,520
Did you hear her scream?

31
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,064
You did great.

32
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:05,690
Could you close it for us too?

33
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,067
- Close it too?
- Yeah.

34
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:08,526
You're so strong.

35
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:10,570
I'll close it.

36
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:16,159
You're now good at this too.

37
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,244
I got it.

38
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:19,871
THEY SUCCESSFULLY CLOSE IT TOO

39
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:22,332
Nice job.

40
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:24,209
Zuha.

41
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:29,005
You can put me
on your shoulders from now on.

42
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:29,964
I did it.

43
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,090
Yeah, keep it up.

44
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:36,846
What? It's open again.

45
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,473
THE DOOR HAS OPENED BY ITSELF

46
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,141
That damn door…

47
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:42,352
THE DAMN DOOR I MADE

48
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,274
One, two…

49
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:54,614
GRUNTING

50
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:55,532
MORE GRUNTING

51
00:01:58,076 --> 00:01:59,160
Hey, let me help.

52
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,371
- Pull me.
- One, two, three.

53
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:04,290
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

54
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:05,917
- Okay.
- One, two, three.

55
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,128
Gosh, that door…

56
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,045
For goodness' sake.

57
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,757
- Should we prepare the ingredients?
- I think so.

58
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,510
LET'S PREPARE DINNER

59
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:17,720
HE SETS UP THE STOOLS

60
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:22,600
TAKES OFF HIS SOCKS IN CASE OF A FLOOD

61
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:25,937
COMPLETELY ADAPTED TO THE KITCHEN

62
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,940
Zuha, it doesn't take long
to make <i>okonomiyaki</i>, right?

63
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:31,192
- But prepping the ingredients take long?
- It does.

64
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,819
I think cooking might take some time.

65
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:33,862
Is that so?

66
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,613
- Maybe about seven minutes?
- Really?

67
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:36,865
Seven minutes per pancake?

68
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,700
All right, let's get started.

69
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,326
My toes…

70
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:43,163
Zuha said we should prepare the cabbage.

71
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:45,498
ZUHA, THE PRIDE OF OSAKA JOINS TOO

72
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:46,416
Is that enough?

73
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:49,669
- Okay.
- How many servings should we make?

74
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:52,630
Well, there were eleven of us yesterday.

75
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,924
And two more guests
are coming today, so it's 13.

76
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,801
Then, 14 servings to be safe?

77
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:57,719
Yeah.

78
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,180
14 PIECES OF <i>OKONOMIYAKI</i>?

79
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,515
It's funny, isn't it?

80
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:03,641
I find it funny too.

81
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:05,018
I'm about to lose my mind.

82
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:07,729
This situation is so funny.
It hits me every once in a while.

83
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,772
WHILE THE EMPLOYEES PREPARE DINNER

84
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:11,733
FIXES HIS PANTS

85
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:16,863
GETS READY FOR THE NEW GUESTS

86
00:03:16,946 --> 00:03:18,615
One for a man, one for a woman.

87
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:22,994
MEANWHILE

88
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:24,621
Why am I going up the mountain?

89
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:26,998
I'm almost there.

90
00:03:27,498 --> 00:03:28,333
That must be it.

91
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:30,501
The red roof.

92
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:34,505
It looks ordinary from the outside.

93
00:03:42,972 --> 00:03:43,973
"Kian's B&B."

94
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,853
A GUEST IN A BLACK COAT APPROACHES

95
00:03:57,862 --> 00:03:59,239
Snow,

96
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,074
grass fields,

97
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,367
a blue sky,

98
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,535
and Kian's B&B.

99
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:07,413
KIAN'S B&B

100
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,123
Why does everything look so big?

101
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:11,542
IT'S BIG FOR REAL

102
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:12,627
It's so big.

103
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,337
What?

104
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:17,173
<i>I was so flustered.</i>

105
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,342
<i>I thought,</i>
<i>"How am I supposed to open this?"</i>

106
00:04:19,425 --> 00:04:21,344
<i>"Should I pray?"</i>

107
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:22,845
<i>There was no one welcoming me.</i>

108
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,222
<i>It was tough.</i>

109
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:28,768
HELLO, MR. KIAN
I'M AT THE FRONT DOOR RIGHT NOW

110
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:32,313
ONE MORE GUEST WILL ARRIVE SOON
YOU CAN OPEN THE DOOR TOGETHER

111
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,399
So you need two people to open the door?

112
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:35,775
I think I can do it by myself.

113
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,277
No, I can't.

114
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:42,323
Someone's there.

115
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:43,491
ANOTHER GUEST ARRIVES

116
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,159
Someone's coming.

117
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:46,953
COMES TO MEET HER HALFWAY

118
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:48,288
Who's that?

119
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,581
Are you a guest?

120
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:51,624
Yes, hello.

121
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,502
Welcome. I arrived a little earlier.

122
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,462
Are you a guest too?

123
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:57,880
Yes, I am.

124
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,677
This is surreal.

125
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,555
Mr. Kian said we need to
work together to open the door.

126
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,140
- Really?
- Yes.

127
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:09,309
WAITING BY THE DOOR

128
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:11,269
- But you know what?
- What?

129
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,021
Can I just open it?

130
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:13,980
Sure.

131
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:15,606
I think…

132
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:16,983
Do you know how to open it?

133
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,235
I think I can just open it like this.

134
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,445
If I do this…

135
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,119
SUCCESSFULLY OPENS THE DOOR

136
00:05:28,202 --> 00:05:30,455
- Hello.
- Hello.

137
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:33,041
- Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

138
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:35,793
Come on in. I'll take that.

139
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:37,879
- I can clean it with you.
- Sorry?

140
00:05:38,629 --> 00:05:39,589
No, you're a guest.

141
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,132
WELCOMES BY CLEANING THE WHEELS

142
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,426
By the way,

143
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,970
everything's huge here.

144
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:49,807
<i>It was like</i> Gulliver's Travels.

145
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,184
<i>Huge hangers,</i>

146
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:52,727
<i>an extremely large TV,</i>

147
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,562
<i>and an extremely large refrigerator.</i>

148
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,564
<i>It was very Kian's B&B-like.</i>

149
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:58,816
This house is so surreal.

150
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,901
Yes.

151
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:01,277
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

152
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,237
- Reverend. Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

153
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,614
Come on in.

154
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:05,615
A PRIEST, NOT A PASTOR

155
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:07,033
What's your name, sir?

156
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:08,326
I'm Min Sang-cheon.

157
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:10,244
- Sang-cheon?
- Yes, Min Sang-cheon.

158
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,245
And your name?

159
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,163
I'm Chae Seul.

160
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:13,498
- Seul?
- Yes, just Seul.

161
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:14,665
Just Seul?

162
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,584
- Hello.
- Hello.

163
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,336
- Hello.
- Hello.

164
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,296
GREETING FROM UP TOP WHILE COOKING

165
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:22,006
<i>I was surprised.</i>

166
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:24,759
<i>Looking at Kian's B&B</i>
<i>from an art director's perspective,</i>

167
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:28,930
<i>I found it really interesting</i>
<i>how they didn't make it about snow</i>

168
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:31,682
<i>just because it was built</i>
<i>in Daegwallyeong.</i>

169
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:34,560
- Where should I unpack my bags?
- The rooms are…

170
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,687
Actually, there are no rooms.

171
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,272
- The whole place is one room.
- Okay.

172
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:39,857
You have no privacy in here.

173
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,651
OPEN SPACE WITHOUT PRIVACY

174
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:43,903
Are there other guests here right now?

175
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,696
They're all out right now.

176
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,616
We have seven other guests at the moment.

177
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:50,493
- That's a lot.
- Yes.

178
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:52,411
And two sleep in the living room.

179
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:55,039
But we need a place to unpack.

180
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,125
- Yes, you need to unpack.
- Yes.

181
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,127
Right now, over there…

182
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:02,630
Next to the <i>ramyeon</i> box.

183
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:04,465
That's the only space left.

184
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:05,967
THE ONLY "PERSONAL SPACE" LEFT

185
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,969
I made a miscalculation.

186
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:10,847
I didn't expect we'd have so many guests.

187
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,140
AN UNEXPECTED SHORTAGE OF BEDS

188
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:13,975
Would you like the corner space?

189
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:16,477
There. It's actually a pretty good spot.

190
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,645
Isn't it taken?

191
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,772
I'm using it, but I can move.

192
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,607
I used it for a day, so I'm sick of it.

193
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,401
I want to sleep somewhere else.

194
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:24,819
BELOW THE HANGERS
BOSS

195
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:25,736
CHAE SEUL

196
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,780
- Then, I'll use this space.
- Okay.

197
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:29,699
NEXT TO <i>RAMYEON</i> BOXES
SANG-CHEON

198
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,951
THE BOSS MOVES AGAIN

199
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:33,244
Right, my luggage.

200
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,330
My luggage…

201
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:41,169
BUT THIS SPACE IS…

202
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:43,254
Then, is she sleeping next to Jun-ho?

203
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:44,422
Is that a bit weird?

204
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:45,548
Don't you think so?

205
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,675
It'd be a bit weird, right?

206
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:49,635
Is a guy using that spot?

207
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,179
- Then, should I go there?
- Then…

208
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:52,763
- Should we switch?
- Should we?

209
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:54,432
- Let's switch.
- Sure.

210
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,726
SANG-CHEON AND SEUL SWITCH

211
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,187
Then, the electric heating pad…

212
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,314
Take one of these.

213
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:02,231
For me? Thank you.

214
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,317
- It's cold at night.
- Thank you.

215
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,401
NEW BEDDINGS PROVIDED

216
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:09,655
Our spots are settled now.

217
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,073
- They are?
- Yes.

218
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,075
Make yourselves comfortable now.

219
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,160
- Sure.
- Yes.

220
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:16,621
You can take your time and look around.

221
00:08:16,704 --> 00:08:17,663
Okay.

222
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,748
MEANWHILE, IN THE KITCHEN

223
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:20,416
We need this for the lotus root.

224
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,918
- We have to grate it?
- Yes.

225
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:26,130
AFTER WASHING HER HANDS

226
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:29,759
STARTS GRATING LOTUS ROOT

227
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:31,844
I'll just slice these right away.

228
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:33,930
Zuha, it's like this, right?

229
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:35,223
LONG STRAND

230
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:36,349
Yes, that looks good.

231
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:38,684
STARTS CUTTING AFTER HER CONFIRMATION

232
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:42,313
IN CHARGE OF KNIFE WORK

233
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:45,191
Is this thin enough for the cabbage?

234
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:49,612
I think it should be a bit thinner.

235
00:08:49,695 --> 00:08:50,613
- Thinner?
- I think so.

236
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:52,198
OKAY, THINNER

237
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:54,534
Or you can just chop those
into smaller pieces.

238
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,244
- Just chop them up more?
- Yes.

239
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:57,453
Just chop it up.

240
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,579
OKAY, SMALLER

241
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,290
INSTRUCTIONS ON SIZE RECEIVED

242
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:05,628
A FLURRY OF CHOPPING

243
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:08,464
Is this a good enough amount?

244
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,674
Yes, that's good.

245
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:10,591
Really? Okay.

246
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,553
THIS TIME, GREEN ONION

247
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:16,138
ONE BY ONE, THOROUGHLY

248
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,975
Is this thin enough? Or make it thinner?

249
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:20,142
It's good enough.

250
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:21,060
- It is? Okay.
- Yes.

251
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:22,979
CHOPPING TASK COMPLETE

252
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:25,523
Right, do we have any sesame oil?

253
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:26,649
Yes, I bought it.

254
00:09:26,732 --> 00:09:27,858
We should make that.

255
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,735
Cabbage dressed in sesame oil.

256
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:30,820
Right, salad.

257
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:31,904
With some sesame seeds.

258
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:34,282
That salad sounds good, right?
It's delicious.

259
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,826
It's so good. Let's add it to the meal.

260
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,495
- I'll tear them up for the salad.
- Okay.

261
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:43,249
SESAME OIL

262
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:45,167
GENEROUSLY

263
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,753
SESAME SEEDS

264
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,547
Did I put in too much oil?

265
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,807
It is supposed to be mild, but…

266
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:03,728
- Maybe it needs soy sauce?
- Should I add some?

267
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:06,147
Or some salt? A little bit of salt.

268
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:07,231
A little bit of salt?

269
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:08,899
TAKES ZUHA'S ADVICE AND ADDS SALT

270
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:15,573
I think salt was the answer.

271
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:19,118
Become delicious.

272
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:20,911
You know "<i>Moe Moe Kyun</i>"?

273
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:21,829
Yeah.

274
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,205
MAGIC SPELL THAT MAKES IT YUMMY

275
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:28,294
THAT'S THE TASTE

276
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:29,545
- Right? It was salt.
- Yeah.

277
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:33,299
It's delicious!

278
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,593
It's delicious. It's ready.

279
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:36,594
CABBAGE SALAD IS DONE

280
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,763
ZUHA LOOKS AT HER PHONE

281
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:41,098
AND STARTS MAKING THE BATTER

282
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:43,809
How much is 300 ml of water?

283
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:44,935
- 300 ml of water?
- Yes.

284
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:46,479
Isn't that 300 ml?

285
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:48,022
- Is it?
- I think so.

286
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:48,939
It's 330 ml.

287
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,233
- Right. You can use that.
- Okay.

288
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:54,612
My mom sent this to me from Japan.

289
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:56,155
- Really?
- It's <i>dashi.</i>

290
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,824
Is it Japanese seasoning powder?

291
00:10:58,908 --> 00:10:59,742
Yes.

292
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:00,951
And the eggs…

293
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:03,621
A LOT OF EGGS

294
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,998
AND ADDS STARCH

295
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:12,421
Are you talking with your mom right now?

296
00:11:13,172 --> 00:11:14,924
I'm asking my mom.

297
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,301
KEEPS ASKING HER MOM WHILE COOKING

298
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,473
THE LOTUS ROOT IS TOO BIG

299
00:11:22,556 --> 00:11:24,141
IT'S OKAY
I'M USING IT TOO

300
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,518
I'M MAKING IT TOO

301
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:28,896
My mom says she's making it right now too.

302
00:11:28,979 --> 00:11:30,147
- Really?
- Yes.

303
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:33,234
I guess she's really worried.

304
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:34,527
Of course, she would be.

305
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,903
You're the pride of Osaka.

306
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:37,863
If you can't make <i>okonomiyaki…</i>

307
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,407
She's teaching her in real time?

308
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,324
- Yes.
- Yeah.

309
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:41,617
She's so sweet.

310
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:43,869
Let's cook it.

311
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,287
THE BATTER IS READY

312
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:46,956
We have three portable stoves now,

313
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,332
so we can make three at a time.

314
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:50,543
- And it takes seven minutes per pancake.
- Right.

315
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:52,420
If we make 13, it'll take a while.

316
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:53,337
AT LEAST 35 MINUTES

317
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,089
Won't the food get all cold?

318
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:59,051
Or we can cook them in advance
and heat them before we serve them.

319
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:00,845
- Like pre-cooking them?
- Yeah.

320
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:02,763
- That's a good idea.
- Right?

321
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,974
We have three pans,
so let's each take one.

322
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,100
- We have three?
- Yeah.

323
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:07,852
- Take this…
- Okay.

324
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,603
- And put it like this.
- Okay.

325
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:12,022
Like pancakes. How should I put it?

326
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,149
Pancakes?

327
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:16,318
LAY DOWN THINLY-SLICED PORK BELLY FIRST

328
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:17,236
It's cooking fast.

329
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:19,196
Just… Don't flip it.

330
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,239
Don't flip it?

331
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,407
Don't flip it.

332
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:24,702
BATTER STRAIGHT ON TOP
WITHOUT FLIPPING PORK BELLY

333
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:27,913
It's like this.

334
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:28,873
- Is this right?
- Yes.

335
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,584
Put the lid on
and wait about three minutes.

336
00:12:34,253 --> 00:12:35,212
Gosh, you brought them.

337
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,338
SECRET WEAPON

338
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,382
- Yes.
- Spatulas for flipping.

339
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:39,800
- It's been three minutes.
- Really?

340
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:41,594
But will we be able to flip them?

341
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,345
GIVING IT A TRY

342
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:45,723
Okay.

343
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:47,266
- In one go?
- Yeah.

344
00:12:50,644 --> 00:12:51,979
- You did it.
- Okay.

345
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:53,981
It looks good.

346
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:56,108
Hey, it looks delicious.

347
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,654
YEON-KOUNG'S TRY

348
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,951
I should've waited.

349
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:07,411
It's good enough.

350
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:08,329
I was so close.

351
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,413
I'll show you.

352
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:10,915
Here I go.

353
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,292
You got it. Okay.

354
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,210
That's good enough.

355
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,338
Put it here.

356
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:19,798
Okay.

357
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,717
THE FIRST BATCH IS DONE

358
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:27,431
11 PANCAKES LEFT TO MAKE NOW

359
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,517
Jun-ho, I'm tired.

360
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,561
Let's change bedtime to 10:00 p.m.

361
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,773
I think we'll end up
going to bed later tonight.

362
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:36,690
We can't.

363
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:38,359
They'll stay up on their last night.

364
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:40,277
No, lights-out is at 11:00 p.m.

365
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:41,529
I don't think it will be.

366
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:44,365
What are you talking about?
It's 11:00 p.m. That's the rule.

367
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,617
You can't change it like that.

368
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,536
So what should we call you? Kian?

369
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:49,912
- Or Mr. Kian?
- Me?

370
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,664
- Whatever you like.
- Whatever?

371
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:53,415
- Let's go with Mr. Kian.
- That seems best.

372
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:54,917
"Mr. Kian"? A bit formal, but okay.

373
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,294
- Then, Kian.
- Then, we'll call you Kian.

374
00:13:57,378 --> 00:14:00,130
I just said whatever you like,
and then you made things awkward.

375
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:03,384
Then, Reverend, are you…

376
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,802
No, I'm a priest.

377
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:05,928
I'm so sorry.

378
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,555
You're a priest. Got it.

379
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:09,848
Both believe in Jesus, but…

380
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:11,642
- I'm sorry.
- It's all right.

381
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:12,768
I'm a Buddhist, so…

382
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:15,854
Well, I noticed you were wearing
a rosary on your wrist.

383
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,648
It's all right. It's no problem at all.

384
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,650
What brought you here?

385
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:22,861
Well, I didn't really have the time
to go traveling.

386
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,405
- Right.
- When I turned 20,

387
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:27,449
I entered a Catholic seminary
to become a priest.

388
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,577
- When you were 20?
- Yes, in college.

389
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,580
I went to a Catholic school
right after high school.

390
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:34,456
I received training for ten years.

391
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,917
During the semester, I lived in the dorms.

392
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,961
During vacations,
we'd go back to our hometowns.

393
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:41,463
But I always had to work
in the church I belonged to,

394
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,841
so I didn't have time to go trips.

395
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:46,218
But after becoming a priest,

396
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:48,596
I can take days off now.

397
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:52,308
And I've realized how fun trips are.

398
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:55,978
As a priest, you don't have
many chances to go on a trip

399
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:57,980
with regular people

400
00:14:58,063 --> 00:15:00,316
and get to know them.

401
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:02,818
Not only was it a challenge
but also a dream for me.

402
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:05,487
- Anyway, I'm not here as a priest.
- Right.

403
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,406
I'm here as a guest and traveler.

404
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:08,782
As a guest?

405
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,243
Are you religious?

406
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,161
I'm not.

407
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:14,705
You're not?
You should pick a faith before you go.

408
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,081
You see,

409
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:18,083
one of the guests is a monk.

410
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:19,543
Is he here right now?

411
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,253
He went to the temple.

412
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:23,297
HE'S HERE NOW

413
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:24,590
KNOCK, KNOCK

414
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,634
Knock, knock.

415
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:29,511
Yes?

416
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:30,638
Could you open the door?

417
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:31,555
Sure.

418
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:35,851
- Hello.
- Hello.

419
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:36,769
Hello.

420
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,729
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

421
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,689
- Are you a priest?
- Yes, I am.

422
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:42,316
I see. Hello.

423
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,109
Are you a monk?

424
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:45,778
No, I'm not a full-fledged one.

425
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:47,154
- I see. Hello.
- Hello.

426
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:48,989
This is a connection,
as Buddhism would say.

427
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:49,990
Thank you.

428
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,576
AFTER GUEST JUN-HO RETURNS

429
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,620
THE FRESHMEN RETURN TOO

430
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:55,955
- They're here.
- There they are.

431
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:58,374
- Someone's here. It's a priest.
- It's a priest.

432
00:15:58,457 --> 00:16:00,459
- Hello.
- Hello.

433
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:02,211
What's up?

434
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:03,337
- Hello.
- Hello.

435
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,380
THE TWINS ARE BACK TOO

436
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:06,298
- Do you need help? Hello.
- Hello.

437
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:09,176
Are you twins?

438
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:10,219
- Yes.
- Yes.

439
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:13,138
- Did you have a good trip?
- Yes, I did.

440
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,181
Most of them are here.

441
00:16:14,264 --> 00:16:15,265
TOTAL 9 GUESTS ON DAY 2

442
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,188
Geez…

443
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,149
- Hi, Boss.
- Hey.

444
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,526
Come on in.

445
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:27,569
- You've made a lot.
- Yes.

446
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,072
Thank you.

447
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:33,242
After we come back,
we can just heat these up

448
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:34,535
when we grill the meat.

449
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:35,452
What time is it?

450
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:37,329
Sunset is at 6:30 p.m.,
so we have an hour.

451
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,248
- Let's go now.
- We should go now.

452
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:42,292
It's either ice sledding or fishing.

453
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,003
So which one?

454
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:46,213
Or they can do whichever one they want.

455
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,756
Let's ask them.

456
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,550
Hey, everyone.

457
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:51,301
Before the sun sets,

458
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:54,555
and since the lake is frozen right now,

459
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,557
we can go fishing

460
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,891
or ice sledding.

461
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,184
So…

462
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:01,770
Does anyone want to go fishing?

463
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,063
Me.

464
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,314
Ice sledding?

465
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,608
Ice sledding.

466
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:09,236
Then, you lead those
who want to go ice sledding.

467
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,821
Okay. Bundle up.

468
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:11,905
Let's go.

469
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,075
LAKE, KIAN'S B&B

470
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,869
THEY ALL GO TO PLAY ON THE ICE

471
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:17,911
ICE SLEDDING

472
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:18,829
Sledding.

473
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:20,706
Watch your step.

474
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:24,376
You went running in the morning too.
Aren't you tired?

475
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,919
No, I'm totally fine.

476
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:29,256
I wanted to do this today as well,
so I'm really excited.

477
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:30,799
That's good.

478
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,968
It's frozen solid.

479
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,178
THEY REACH THE FROZEN LAKE

480
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:35,095
Oh, my gosh.

481
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,889
- This is amazing.
- Yeah.

482
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:41,185
A BIG LAKE NEAR KIAN'S B&B

483
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:46,106
THE BOSS FOUND IT WHEN HE FIRST VISITED

484
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:47,566
Is it okay to do ice fishing?

485
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,193
Yes, they said it's okay.

486
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:50,986
It must be really deep in the middle.

487
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:51,904
About 40 m?

488
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,822
That sounds about right.

489
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:58,160
HE TASTES THE WATER

490
00:17:58,243 --> 00:17:59,912
What should we do here?

491
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:01,580
<i>When I saw it,</i>

492
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:03,665
<i>I wanted to fish</i>
<i>while looking at the scenery</i>

493
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:05,042
<i>and go sledding.</i>

494
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:07,461
<i>Here, the guests can enjoy</i>

495
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:09,671
a different kind of experience outside.

496
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:12,174
That's why I planned it this way.

497
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:15,094
THE FLOWING LAKE

498
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:18,263
IS FROZEN SOLID NOW

499
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:20,766
A SNOW-WHITE PLAYGROUND

500
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:22,392
I wouldn't have known this was a lake.

501
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,103
- It just looks like frozen land.
- Right?

502
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:26,563
This is incredible!

503
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:29,358
- It's so cool here.
- I know.

504
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:32,152
Come, and each take one.

505
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:34,446
YEON-KOUNG IS IN CHARGE OF ICE SLEDDING

506
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,240
Two holes should be enough.

507
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:37,449
BOSS IS IN CHARGE OF FISHING

508
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:38,826
Here, take this.

509
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:40,369
FISHING TEAM, SLEDDING TEAM

510
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:41,328
This way for fishing.

511
00:18:44,915 --> 00:18:46,333
EXCITED

512
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,586
There we go. Gosh, the water.

513
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:50,504
FISHING HOLE OPENED

514
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:51,713
- Two people per hole.
- Okay.

515
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,048
- Sounds good.
- Here?

516
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:54,550
ONE MORE HOLE FOR THE TWINS

517
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:56,552
AMAZED

518
00:18:58,137 --> 00:18:59,304
The ice is thick.

519
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,932
THE ICE IS ABOUT 30 CM THICK

520
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,811
SHALL WE GET STARTED?

521
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:08,147
Hold on, why does it keep doing this?

522
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:10,357
- How do you do this?
- What?

523
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,817
Is this your first time fishing?

524
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,235
- Yes.
- It is?

525
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,903
Take this and… Look.

526
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:16,613
Don't unwind it all.

527
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,073
MR. KIAN'S FISHING CLASS

528
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:19,366
Take an earthworm.

529
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,911
Is it alive?

530
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:24,705
There. I put it to sleep.

531
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:26,540
I'm sorry.

532
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:29,168
HOW TO ICE FISH
1. PUT BAIT TO SLEEP

533
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,170
Now, bait the hook.

534
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:32,504
2. STICK ON THE BAIT WELL

535
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:33,422
Stick it on.

536
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:35,132
Bait the hook. Now, look.

537
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,593
Put it in the water.

538
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,469
Take the rod, and do this.

539
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,929
3. LURE FISH WITH MOVEMENT

540
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,181
Up and down.

541
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,725
If a fish bites it, you'll feel it.

542
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:46,768
- Okay.
- When that happens, just pull.

543
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:48,562
4. TIME IT RIGHT AND PULL

544
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:50,772
You baited the hook? Nice.

545
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:51,899
CHAE SEUL HAS EXPERIENCE

546
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:53,734
But are there fish in the water?

547
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,612
Yes. Apparently, there are masu salmon.

548
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:58,363
SMELT AND MASU SALMON LIVE HERE

549
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,365
How long does it usually take?

550
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:02,367
Sometimes, you catch something right away.

551
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:04,953
Sometimes, you don't catch anything
for three days.

552
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,038
For three days?

553
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:07,080
Or four days.

554
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:09,458
Just relax and enjoy the scenery too.

555
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:12,002
It's exciting when your hands
feel a fish on the line.

556
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:13,170
My hands?

557
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:14,630
OKAY, GOT IT

558
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:15,923
Come to us.

559
00:20:17,841 --> 00:20:19,718
It's no fun if we don't catch anything.

560
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:22,471
We need to get a nibble at least.

561
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,140
Everyone, hurry up and get on.

562
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:26,475
- Two more.
- Two?

563
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,559
MEANWHILE, SLEDDING TEAM

564
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:28,894
Is that how you ride it?

565
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:30,103
Should we get on our knees?

566
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:32,022
GRUNTING

567
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,232
It goes pretty smoothly.

568
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,113
THE SPIRIT OF A 20-YEAR-OLD
POWERING THROUGH

569
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,531
Let's go.

570
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:43,200
JUN-HO PUSHES YEON-KOUNG

571
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:45,911
This is fun!

572
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,831
- Sit tight.
- Okay.

573
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:51,500
Thank you!

574
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:53,919
I never imagined this day would come.
My gosh!

575
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,757
Should we have a race or something?

576
00:20:58,840 --> 00:20:59,675
A race?

577
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:00,634
A contest?

578
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,094
- Are we doing a race?
- Count me in!

579
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:03,303
A RACE? COUNT ME IN!

580
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:04,846
- Should I join too?
- You four.

581
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:07,099
Hey, don't cross the line.

582
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:08,558
Up to here, right?

583
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:09,476
No, you can't.

584
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:10,894
Okay, are you ready?

585
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,062
KIAN'S B&B'S SLEDDING RACE

586
00:21:12,145 --> 00:21:13,063
Ready.

587
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,856
Get set, go!

588
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:16,692
Go!

589
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:17,818
YEON-KOUNG

590
00:21:17,901 --> 00:21:20,237
No, wait!

591
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:24,157
Hey, this is like the Winter Olympics.

592
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,075
COMPETITIVE SPIRIT

593
00:21:25,158 --> 00:21:26,535
I'm going to win the gold medal.

594
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:28,161
COMPETITIVE YEON-KOUNG TAKES THE LEAD

595
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:32,791
She's catching up!

596
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,084
ZUHA'S SURGING AHEAD?

597
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:35,502
She's catching up!

598
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:37,629
CLENCHING HER TEETH

599
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,849
- She's catching up!
- I won!

600
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:51,143
YEON-KOUNG, 1ST PLACE

601
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:52,311
- First place!
- First place!

602
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,021
- She won!
- The winner!

603
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:57,232
SO CLOSE

604
00:21:57,983 --> 00:22:00,527
PANTING

605
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,195
One more.

606
00:22:02,279 --> 00:22:04,281
Gosh, I'm not good at this.

607
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:06,742
MEN'S DIVISION MATCH

608
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:09,036
- Hold on.
- Here. This is the line.

609
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,412
STRICT

610
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,706
Someone signal the start.

611
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:13,874
Zuha will do it.

612
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:15,917
AHEM

613
00:22:16,001 --> 00:22:17,544
She's suddenly clearing her throat.

614
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,296
Ready!

615
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:22,966
Get set, go!

616
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:25,594
Get set, go!

617
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:29,598
No way!

618
00:22:30,348 --> 00:22:31,558
TRYING HARD

619
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,393
- Hey, Lee Jun-ho!
- Lee Jun-ho!

620
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:36,605
JUN-HO

621
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:38,815
Lee Jun-ho!

622
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,401
- First, second, third, fourth, fifth.
- Goal!

623
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,569
OVERWHELMING VICTORY

624
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:44,446
NICE JOB, JUN-HO

625
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:45,781
He's the winner.

626
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:48,241
- I got the gold medal.
- Nice job.

627
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:52,829
- Lee Jun-ho!
- Lee Jun-ho!

628
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:54,247
BOISTEROUS

629
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:55,165
Goal!

630
00:22:57,084 --> 00:22:58,960
They're so noisy. We're fishing here.

631
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:02,339
They're quite annoying, aren't they?

632
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:03,256
ANNOYING?

633
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,258
- They're bothering us.
- Right.

634
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:06,927
Do they own the place or something?

635
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:08,929
What's going on?

636
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:10,680
Come on out.

637
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:13,433
STUDYING THEIR FACES

638
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:14,351
Geez.

639
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:16,394
RESTLESS AND WORRIED

640
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,939
What does it feel like
when something bites?

641
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:21,608
You'll know it when a fish bites.

642
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:24,194
Once we catch something,

643
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:25,654
we'll have way more fun than them.

644
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:26,571
Really?

645
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:29,491
It's crazy.
You'll want to go fishing every day.

646
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:31,701
WANTING THEM TO EXPERIENCE IT

647
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:35,122
I feel some kind of movement.

648
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:37,415
Nibbles. He said we'd feel nibbles.

649
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:38,667
THE NIBBLES HE MENTIONED?

650
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:43,922
FINALLY A BITE?

651
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:45,382
I think it brushed by.

652
00:23:45,465 --> 00:23:46,299
What?

653
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:51,930
THIS FEELING!

654
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:55,517
NOTHING BUT THE BAIT

655
00:23:56,143 --> 00:23:57,144
Darn it.

656
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:03,733
DISAPPOINTED

657
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,068
Maybe they're hibernating.

658
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:09,781
You're supposed to do this
while listening to quiet sounds of nature.

659
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:13,577
We have such quiet sounds of nature today.

660
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:17,414
VERY QUIET SOUNDS OF NATURE

661
00:24:17,497 --> 00:24:20,083
Lee Jun-ho!

662
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,918
Kim Yeon-koung!

663
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:28,842
IN DIFFERENT WORLDS

664
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:31,761
Why do I feel so angry?

665
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:34,097
It's annoying enough to not get any bites.

666
00:24:35,473 --> 00:24:36,433
GLANCING

667
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:38,059
Smita's turned her back.

668
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:39,728
LOSS OF INTEREST

669
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:41,354
I bet this is her last time fishing.

670
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,814
- Her first and last.
- Yeah.

671
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:45,775
Most people never do it again
when their first time goes like this.

672
00:24:45,859 --> 00:24:47,485
- Do you want to do that?
- Sorry?

673
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:50,113
You don't have to do this.
You can join them.

674
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,031
- We're okay.
- Really?

675
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:52,532
- Yes.
- All right.

676
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:53,617
We are okay.

677
00:24:54,951 --> 00:24:56,953
You all look lonely here.

678
00:24:57,537 --> 00:24:59,372
- Keep it down, will you?
- Yeah.

679
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:00,957
All the fish are running away.

680
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,292
TAKING IT OUT ON HIM

681
00:25:02,375 --> 00:25:03,251
They're running away?

682
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:06,087
Yes, because you're being so noisy.

683
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,131
Should we stop?

684
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:09,466
Have you given up?

685
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:10,717
- What?
- Have you given up?

686
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:13,511
No, not giving up.
We're just wrapping it up beautifully.

687
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,972
- It was fun.
- It's nice that we didn't kill anything.

688
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,516
Right, let's wrap it up beautifully.

689
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:21,353
<i>I'd never been</i>

690
00:25:21,436 --> 00:25:23,730
<i>on the ice like that before in my life.</i>

691
00:25:23,813 --> 00:25:25,232
<i>It was such a nice experience.</i>

692
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:28,026
After going fishing,
that was our first and last time.

693
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:28,944
That's it.

694
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:30,028
Let's go!

695
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:31,363
<i>It felt like a dream.</i>

696
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:34,157
<i>I'd never tried it before,</i>
<i>so it was even better.</i>

697
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:38,161
<i>I looked at the distant mountains</i>
<i>as I rode the sled,</i>

698
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:39,454
<i>and the sun was setting.</i>

699
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:40,538
<i>It was so romantic.</i>

700
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:41,873
THE DEFINITION OF ROMANTIC

701
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,627
- Let's put away the things we brought.
- Okay.

702
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:47,045
Okay, let's wrap it up.

703
00:25:47,128 --> 00:25:48,338
That was so much fun.

704
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:52,384
We picked the wrong fishing spot.

705
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:54,636
I bet the food's getting cold.

706
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:55,595
LET'S GO EAT

707
00:25:55,679 --> 00:25:56,930
Let's grill some meat.

708
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:00,058
Damn it.

709
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:04,312
BACK TO PREPARING DINNER

710
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,939
Tonight is your last night?

711
00:26:06,022 --> 00:26:07,691
- It's tomorrow night.
- Tomorrow?

712
00:26:07,774 --> 00:26:09,109
- That's good.
- It is?

713
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:10,652
It's good that we're leaving?

714
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:12,821
No, it's good
that tonight isn't your last night.

715
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:13,905
FLUSTERED

716
00:26:13,989 --> 00:26:16,408
Hey, why are you getting offended?

717
00:26:17,033 --> 00:26:18,285
You said that was good.

718
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:20,412
Yes, it's good
that you're here one more day.

719
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:22,163
- Okay.
- Because it would've been a shame.

720
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:24,124
- Okay.
- You're not that bad.

721
00:26:25,375 --> 00:26:26,710
Do you want an Indian name?

722
00:26:26,793 --> 00:26:27,752
Give me one.

723
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,004
- Really?
- Yeah.

724
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:31,423
I have one for you.

725
00:26:33,008 --> 00:26:34,092
What is it?

726
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:35,051
Sukhwinder.

727
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:36,303
Skowinde?

728
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:37,262
Sukhwinder.

729
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:38,346
Skwindle?

730
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:39,973
- Sukh…
- Sukh…

731
00:26:40,056 --> 00:26:41,474
- …winder.
- …winder.

732
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:42,559
Sukhwinder.

733
00:26:42,642 --> 00:26:43,810
- Yes.
- What does it mean?

734
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:45,729
What does it mean? It means…

735
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:46,980
A person who fights.

736
00:26:49,482 --> 00:26:50,775
But that's too cool for me.

737
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:53,903
- No, really.
- I'm honestly not that manly.

738
00:26:53,987 --> 00:26:55,905
I'm pretty feminine.

739
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:57,907
- Really?
- Yes, feminine.

740
00:26:57,991 --> 00:26:59,492
FEMININE BOSS

741
00:26:59,576 --> 00:27:01,077
I have a bit of a feminine side.

742
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:01,995
You do.

743
00:27:02,078 --> 00:27:03,246
Yeah, as I get older…

744
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:06,333
FEMININE WARRIOR

745
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:07,375
Is rice okay?

746
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:08,543
I'm glad you're here.

747
00:27:08,626 --> 00:27:11,171
After I put rice on the trays,
you can put this.

748
00:27:11,254 --> 00:27:12,088
Got it.

749
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:18,845
IN CHARGE OF SERVING THE FOOD
KIAN AND JUN-HO

750
00:27:18,928 --> 00:27:20,513
IN CHARGE OF OKONOMIYAKI
ZUHA

751
00:27:23,725 --> 00:27:26,061
It does smell like <i>okonomiyaki.</i>

752
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:28,605
IN CHARGE OF GRILLING
YEON-KOUNG

753
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:30,482
I like them crisp.
Can I grill them that way?

754
00:27:30,565 --> 00:27:31,399
Of course.

755
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:34,402
THE MEAT IS READY TOO

756
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:37,030
Excuse me, could you help me out?

757
00:27:37,113 --> 00:27:37,947
Okay.

758
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:41,159
Everyone, come take your food.

759
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,077
Thank you.

760
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:46,831
If you need more,
we'll bring some more down.

761
00:27:47,415 --> 00:27:48,500
They grilled a lot of meat.

762
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:50,293
CABBAGE SALAD, PORK BELLY, OKONOMIYAKI

763
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:51,544
PLENTY OF EXTRA FOOD

764
00:27:51,628 --> 00:27:52,754
This is a lot.

765
00:27:53,546 --> 00:27:54,506
Okay, come and sit.

766
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:57,217
- Take your seats.
- You can sit wherever you want.

767
00:27:58,885 --> 00:28:00,345
We always end up like this.

768
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:02,138
SITTING IN A CIRCLE

769
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:03,848
- We're wrapping up the day.
- Right.

770
00:28:04,474 --> 00:28:06,309
- Tell them about your <i>okonomiyaki.</i>
- Yeah.

771
00:28:06,393 --> 00:28:07,560
My <i>okonomiyaki?</i>

772
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:08,645
What should I say?

773
00:28:08,728 --> 00:28:10,271
It's a famous dish from Osaka.

774
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:12,148
- It's Osaka-style, right?
- Right.

775
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:15,944
I wanted to try making it,
so I learned it from my mom in Japan.

776
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:18,154
But I'm not sure about the taste.

777
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:20,365
- It'll be good.
- Please try some.

778
00:28:20,448 --> 00:28:21,491
Please enjoy.

779
00:28:21,574 --> 00:28:23,076
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

780
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:24,411
Thank you for the food.

781
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:39,050
<i>It felt like I was being judged,</i>
<i>so I was nervous.</i>

782
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:46,349
It's really good.

783
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:48,059
It's so good.

784
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:50,145
It's better than what I had in Osaka.

785
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:51,688
You're a good cook.

786
00:28:51,771 --> 00:28:52,897
- Really?
- Yeah.

787
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:54,107
That's a relief.

788
00:28:56,025 --> 00:28:57,110
It's good.

789
00:28:59,612 --> 00:29:02,907
So you came here and got ready
before the first guests arrived?

790
00:29:02,991 --> 00:29:03,908
Yes.

791
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:07,620
After we had lunch yesterday,
that's when we started getting calls.

792
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:09,080
We never knew so many would come.

793
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:10,081
Right.

794
